#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/lb.rc -- Luxembourgish (Lëtzebuergesch), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "lb"`.
//
// Stage E109, group B: an adaptation of en.rc and ru.rc, not a word-for-word translation (decision 198.14).
// The two string tables of the language -- the dialog block and the menu block -- in the order of en.rc;
// the glossary of the language is l10n\glossary\lb.tsv of the control contour. The rules every table obeys
// stand in app.rc above the #include lines; where each string is seen and how much room it has is
// res/lang/context.tsv; tests/l10n.rs holds this file to en.rc.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Luxembourgish — `[general] language = "lb"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
